      },
      {
        "_uid": "207ffe954df153cd",
        "component": "news_media",
        "role": "richtext",
        "filename": "2806-richtext-204856b418-Celebrating-Grandparents.pdf",
        "src": "/news-media/2806-richtext-204856b418-Celebrating-Grandparents.pdf",
        "media_type": "other",
        "caption": "Celebrating Grandparents.pdf",
        "alt": "Children's e-book launched to encourage compassion for the elderly",
        "source_key": "/sonampk/research/SiteAssets/Lists/Geriatrics and Gerontology/AllItems/Celebrating Grandparents.pdf"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\"Celebrating Grandparents\", a literary collaboration between the Aga Khan University School of Nursing and Midwifery, AKU-SONAM, and the department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, AKUH, was recently launched by faculty members, for children of ages 8-11 years.  "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The e-book is co-authored by "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Laila Akber Cassum",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "https://www.aku.edu/sonampk/faculty/pages/profile.aspx?ProfileID=68",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", senior instructor and head of the Geriatric and Gerontology Clinical Stream at AKU-SONAM and "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Dr Shelina Bhamani",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "https://www.aku.edu/mcpk/faculty/pages/profile.aspx?ProfileID=811",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", Early Childhood Development (ECD), Parenting Education Programme lead and assistant professor, Research at AKU."
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\"I know how vulnerable elderly people can become, feeling like a burden in their own house sometimes, which can adversely affect their mental health,\" said Laila Akber Cassum. \"That's why I decided to write an exciting book for children. I believe that stories can serve as a powerful tool to connect two generations together and plant the seeds of our lost socio-cultural values for family elders. Everyone in this society will have to play their part whether they are parents and families, schoolteachers, ECD experts or health care professionals.\" "
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "With engaging content that highlights the importance of grandparents in the lives of grandchildren, the book aims to teach young kids about the joys of cherishing their grandparents and treating them with love and respect. The book was beautifully illustrated by Maria Riaz, edited by Maliha Fazal and Umaima Mughal and the content reviewed by Dr Marie Andrades."
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Sharing why this e-book was meaningful for her, Dr Shelina Bhamani said, \"The periods of early and later childhood set the trajectory for a lifelong aptitude. Today children are spending a lot of time on their screens that's why we opted for an e-book. It's easier to create a positive change through children rather than adults. Sometimes, kids can even teach the right things to their parents because they believe in it with all their heart.\""
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Dr Farid Panjwani, dean of the AKU Institute for Educational Development, AKU-IED, was the chief guest at the book launch ceremony. Other speakers included Dr Lumaan Sheikh, chairof department of Ob/Gyn, MC; Dr Salman Kirmani, chair of division of Women & Child Health, MC; and Dr Rozina Karmaliani, dean of SONAM. They praised the efforts of the authors and firmly affirmed the vital need for public advocacy on this topic."
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " The e-book is available online free of cost. "
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Download the e-book >>",
              "marks": [
                {
